<section class="placeholder-text container">
  <p>
    But while the core housing process has remained the same, special interest housing (SIH), program and theme housing has changed. More specifically, those applying for SIH are guaranteed placement but cannot decline participation in this process once accepted, and residents of theme-based housing (barring Greek and the Substance Free or Recovery Community) are now selected in a randomized lottery instead of by the respective houses’ leadership groups.
  </p>
  <p>
    Eno Thomson-Tribe ’29 applied to the Environmental Program House (EPH), The Wellness Center’s residence hall at Sternlicht Commons and to be a Community Coordinator (CC) for first-year students, the latter of which live in residence halls for freshmen. He was rejected by all three and as such, will now enter general selection.
  </p>
  <p>
    When asked about the application process for EPH and the Wellness Center’s housing in an interview with The Herald, Thomson-Tribe said that it was “deceptively simple.”
  </p>
</section>

